[Applause]  [Music]  the northerners in their islands were  disturbed taken away in the fray not one  stood before their hands from Quetta  code a car commish  Arvid a Lhasa they were wasted they set  up a camp in one place in a more they  desolated his people and his land like  that which is not  they came with fire prepared before them  forward to Egypt their main support was  Pella set theko shekel Esch denyen and  wish these lands were united and they  laid their hands upon the land as far as  the circle of the earth their hearts  were confident full of their plans King  Ramses the third the king himself he  says hearken to me all the land gathered  in one place the court the King's  children the butler's the youth all the  young men who are in this land give your  attention to my utterance that you may  know my plans for sustaining you alive  the new may learn of the might of my  father aim on creator of my beauty his  great might victorious against every  fallen foe beneath my feet he decrees to  me victory and his hand is with me so  that every invader of my boundary is  slain in my grasp his chosen one whom he  found among hundreds of thousands not a  single man among them to rescue them  from the  beause I surrounded her I established  her by my valiant mite when I arose like  the Sun as king over Egypt I protected  her I expelled for her the nine Mo's now  it happened through this God the Lord of  gods that I was prepared and armed to  trap them like wild fowl he furnished my  strength and caused my plans to prosper  I went forth directing these marvelous  things I equipped my frontier in za he  prepared before them the Chiefs the  captain of infantry the nobles I caused  to equip the Harbor mouths like a strong  wall with warships galleys and barges  they were manned completely from bow to  stern with valiant warriors bearing  their arms soldiers of all the choicest  of Egypt being like the lions roaring  upon the mountaintops the charioteers  were warriors and all good officers  ready at hand their horses were  quivering in their every limb ready to  crush the countries under their feet I  was the valiant Amon - stationed before  them that they might behold the  hand-to-hand fighting of my arms I King  Ramses the third was made a farce  striding hero conscious of his might  valiant to lead his army in the day of  battle  those who reached my boundary their seed  is not their heart and their soul are  finished forever and ever as for those  who had assembled before them on the see  the full flame was in their front before  the harbour mouths and a wall of metal  upon the shore surrounded them they were  dragged overturned and laid low upon the  beach slain and made heaps from Stern to  bow of their galleys but all their  things were cast upon the water then I  turned back the waters in remembrance of  Egypt when they mentioned my name in  their land made consume them while I sit  upon the throne of her Oktay and the  serpent diadem is fixed upon my head  like rah I permit not the countries to  see the boundaries of Egypt as for the  nine bows I have taken away their land  and their boundaries they are added to  mine their chiefs and their people come  to me with praise I carried out the  plans of the all Lord the August divine  Father Lord of the Gods their hands are  for me the shield of my body to ward off  evil and misfortune from my limbs the  king ruler of the nine bows Lord of the  two lands Rameses the third given life  stability satisfaction like rah for ever  and ever  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

